            <ArticleTitle>Projected complex sensations after interscalene brachial plexus block.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1270-1, table of contents</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="IMPLICATIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The development of projected complex sensations mimicking phantom pain after interscalene block is reported. The recognition of this entity is important because it may be confused with some other cardiac, esophageal, or visceral pathologies.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
